{
  "rules": [
    "Strong persistent underprediction in rising regimes: when the last 5–10 days show an upswing/breakout, add an upward bias that grows with horizon (small in week 1, larger by weeks 3–4).",
    "Trend/level lag: forecasts follow the prior range (~68–72) while outcomes reprice to a higher plateau (~75–83). Use a regime-shift detector (e.g., close > recent 20d high) to step the whole path upward rather than gradual drift.",
    "Horizon-specific bias: error increases monotonically with lead time; apply an increasing correction factor with horizon (e.g., +X €/t in days 1–7, +2X in days 8–14, +3X in days 15–30) during uptrends.",
    "Over-mean-reversion: model repeatedly pulls back toward ~69–71 even as realized prices keep trending up. Reduce mean-reversion strength (or increase trend weight) when realized volatility is elevated and price is making higher highs.",
    "Post-spike behavior mis-modeled: after upside acceleration, the model expects a pullback/flattening too early; delay any reversion/flattening signal until at least several closes below a short-term moving average (e.g., 5–10d)."
  ]
}
